From: Jiacheng Yu <yujiacheng3@huawei.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:28:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH OLK-6.6 v5 00/18] MOC bypass cache

The MOC (MemoryOnChip) bypass cache feature uses the Arm Page Based Hardware
Attributes (PBHA, FEAT_HPDS2) to describe per-mapping performance hints.
MOC memory is not cached in the system cache, so the OS has to be told which
pages may be mapped with the MOC attribute.

This series adds:
 - stage1 PBHA support, discovered from the device tree or from the EFI stub
 - KVM stage2 support, including the VTCR_EL2.PBHA override mask
 - page based control: PROT_PBHA_BIT0, VM_PBHA_BIT0, prctl and
   /proc/<pid>/pbha_bit0
 - the pbha= boot parameter and the MOC mode plumbing in the EFI stub

Based on OLK-6.6.

Changes in v5:
 - move the /proc/<pid>/pbha_bit0 implementation to fs/proc/pbha.c; base.c
   only registers the entry

Changes in v4:
 - restore %ld when printing the static key state; %d broke the aarch64
   build with -Werror=format

Changes in v3:
 - dt-bindings: update the six stale references to arm/cpu.yaml, add the
   maintainers entry and fix the description
 - fix the for-loop style in the PBHA parsing code
 - move pbha.rst to Documentation/arch/arm64/
 - use a free vm_flags bit for VM_PBHA_BIT0 and document the p0 mnemonic
 - drop the set_huge_pte_at() find_vma() lookup; the hint is carried by
   vm_page_prot
 - rewrite a live THP pmd through pmdp_invalidate_ad()
 - take an mm reference in pbha_bit0_read()
 - add a .hugetlb_entry callback so /proc/<pid>/pbha_bit0 and prctl update
   hugetlb mappings as well
 - limit the global-init flagging to current->mm
 - base the "nothing to do" decision on the actual VMA state instead of
   mm->def_flags
 - reject a NULL or unrecognized pbha= value


Fanhua Li (2):
  arm64: mm: Set PBHA0 bit for VM_PBHA_BIT0
  arm64: mm: Introduce procfs interface to update PBHA0 bit

James Morse (7):
  KVM: arm64: Detect and enable PBHA for stage2
  dt-bindings: Rename the description of cpu nodes cpu.yaml
  dt-bindings: arm: Add binding for Page Based Hardware Attributes
  arm64: cpufeature: Enable PBHA bits for stage1
  arm64: mm: Add pgprot_pbha() to allow drivers to request PBHA values
  KVM: arm64: Configure PBHA bits for stage2
  Documentation: arm64: Describe the support and expectations for PBHA

Ma Wupeng (9):
  arm64: cpufeature: Enable PBHA for stage1 early via FDT
  arm64: mm: Detect and enable PBHA bit0 at early startup
  arm64: mm: Update kernel pte entries if pbha bit0 enabled
  arm64: mm: Show PBHA bit 59 as PBHA0 in ptdump
  arm64: mm: Introduce VM_PBHA_BIT0 to enable pbha bit0 for single vma
  arm64: mm: Set flag VM_PBHA_BIT0 for global init task
  arm64: mm: Introduce prctl to control pbha behavior
  arm64: mm: Introduce kernel param pbha
  openeuler: configs: arm64: Enable PBHA by default

